    "narrative": "For LawDog today, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as the most compelling start, boasting an elite 62.96 score. Despite a challenging matchup against Sonny Gray (xERA 3.89), **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost due to the platoon advantage and a park factor that tilts heavily in his favor. While his projected spot in the 8-hole drags his efficiency down, the underlying power metrics make him a must-start as we chase counting stats. **Cal Raleigh** remains a high-floor play at 59.62, bolstered by favorable wind conditions at the park, while **Masyn Winn** (56.37) continues to be an essential anchor given our focus on speed and his solid matchup against Assad.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the cutoff with a score of 36.49. While his versatility as a switch-hitter is valuable, he fell below the 40-point efficiency floor due to a tough matchup against Weathers (xERA 3.41), whose high strikeout floor suppresses the ceiling for a hitter currently fighting for consistent production. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Luis Arraez**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **JJ Bleday**. Because those six players have \"Lineup Pending\" tags, our projections\u2014particularly for **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Drew Gilbert**, who face the tricky JP Sears\u2014are subject to volatility. If **Jung Hoo Lee** or **Drew Gilbert** are dropped out of their respective lineup spots, we will be forced to reconsider their utility to preserve game caps, especially given the difficulty of facing JP Sears today.",
